WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:07.008
The next morning Miles was about to leave when Edward woke up.

2
00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:15.575
"Where are you going?" Edward said in a sleepy voice. "I'm freezing."

3
00:00:15.576 --> 00:00:19.909
"I'm just going out to run an errand," Miles replied.

4
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:24.421
"You'll be warmer if you pull the covers over your head."

5
00:00:24.422 --> 00:00:31.326
Too tired to order Miles to do that for him, Edward just grunted and tugged on the covers.

6
00:00:31.327 --> 00:00:37.573
Half an hour later, Miles returned with some secondhand clothes for Edward.

7
00:00:37.574 --> 00:00:42.881
Made of cheap material, they clearly showed signs of wear.

8
00:00:42.882 --> 00:00:49.740
"At least they're clean and warm, and I can mend the smaller holes," Miles thought.

9
00:00:49.741 --> 00:00:52.948
"I hope they're the right size."

10
00:00:52.949 --> 00:00:58.960
Miles held up a shirt and compared it to the lump in the bed across the room.

11
00:00:58.961 --> 00:01:04.802
He sat down and took out a needle and thread.

12
00:01:04.803 --> 00:01:10.626
It took him five tries, but at last he succeeded in threading the needle.

13
00:01:10.627 --> 00:01:15.100
Miles hummed quietly while he worked on his mending.

14
00:01:15.101 --> 00:01:20.074
"Ouch! That's a sharp needle!" Miles said aloud.

15
00:01:20.075 --> 00:01:24.390
He sucked his finger as he looked over at the bed.

16
00:01:24.391 --> 00:01:27.877
Edward did not stir.

17
00:01:27.878 --> 00:01:31.879
"Poor lad must be exhausted," he thought.

18
00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:37.010
"I'll have to wake him soon, so we can eat and be on our way to Hendon Hall."

19
00:01:37.011 --> 00:01:42.668
Miles wished he had more money, so that he could afford better clothes for Edward.

20
00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:45.090
But these would have to do.

21
00:01:45.091 --> 00:01:49.394
He still needed to pay for their food and lodging along the way.

22
00:01:49.395 --> 00:01:53.558
Finished with the mending, Miles called Edward.

23
00:01:53.559 --> 00:01:56.664
"Time to get up, Your Majesty!"

24
00:01:56.665 --> 00:02:01.399
There was still no sign of life from the lump in the bed.

25
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:06.659
Miles finally approached the bed and threw back the covers. "Edward?"

26
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.132
The boy was gone!

27
00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:13.417
Miles looked around the small room.

28
00:02:13.418 --> 00:02:17.481
There was no place for Edward to hide.

29
00:02:17.482 --> 00:02:21.046
Just then someone knocked at the door.

30
00:02:21.047 --> 00:02:26.963
Miles opened it, expecting Edward, but a servant pushed past him with breakfast.

31
00:02:26.964 --> 00:02:33.650
"Not so fast!" Miles said. "Have you seen the boy who was with me?"

32
00:02:33.651 --> 00:02:38.220
The servant laid the dishes on the table. "Um—"

33
00:02:38.221 --> 00:02:42.329
"Where is he?" Miles demanded.

34
00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:46.923
"Soon after you left, a young man came to the inn."

35
00:02:46.924 --> 00:02:50.566
The servant anxiously wrung his hands.

36
00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:56.439
"He said that you wanted the boy to meet you in the woods beyond the bridge.

37
00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.897
So I brought the young man to your room.

38
00:02:59.898 --> 00:03:04.193
He woke up the lad and delivered his message."

39
00:03:04.194 --> 00:03:10.429
"And what did the boy say to that? I can't imagine he was very happy."

40
00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:18.001
"Well, he did grumble about being disturbed 'so early,' as he put it.

41
00:03:18.002 --> 00:03:22.337
But he left with the young man right away.

42
00:03:22.338 --> 00:03:29.467
On the way out, he remarked that you showed bad manners in sending a stranger instead of coming yourself."

43
00:03:29.468 --> 00:03:35.890
"I didn't send a stranger, you fool!" Miles began to pace the room.

44
00:03:35.891 --> 00:03:38.468
"Perhaps no harm will come to the boy.

45
00:03:38.469 --> 00:03:41.293
I'll eat and then I'll go in search of him.

46
00:03:41.294 --> 00:03:45.142
Quick! Set the table. No, wait!"

47
00:03:45.143 --> 00:03:53.571
Miles stopped pacing. "Someone tried to make it look like the boy was still in bed. Why?"

48
00:03:53.572 --> 00:04:01.292
"I don't know for sure," the servant said, "but I saw the young man fooling with the covers."

49
00:04:01.293 --> 00:04:05.281
"It's clear that someone wanted to deceive me."

50
00:04:05.282 --> 00:04:08.895
Miles smacked his forehead with his hand.

51
00:04:08.896 --> 00:04:15.143
"Whoever it was wanted to gain time so they could escape. Was the young man alone?"

52
00:04:15.144 --> 00:04:18.615
"Yes, all alone."

53
00:04:18.616 --> 00:04:23.962
"Are you sure?" Miles persisted. "Think hard."

54
00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:27.870
The servant wrinkled his brow as if that would help him think.

55
00:04:27.871 --> 00:04:33.730
"Oh! Now I remember! No one came here with the young man.

56
00:04:33.731 --> 00:04:39.279
But I happened to be looking out the window when he and the boy reached the bridge."

57
00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:43.367
"What happened then?" Miles thundered impatiently.

58
00:04:43.368 --> 00:04:45.673
"Just then the innkeeper called me—"

59
00:04:45.674 --> 00:04:49.781
"No, no! What happened to the boy?"

60
00:04:49.782 --> 00:04:54.797
"A man dressed in rags stepped out of the shadows and followed them."

61
00:04:54.798 --> 00:04:57.843
"Did you get a good look at him?"

62
00:04:57.844 --> 00:05:04.157
"His arm was in a sling, and he had a patch over one eye."

63
00:05:04.158 --> 00:05:07.846
Miles sat down at the table and rubbed his eyes.

64
00:05:07.847 --> 00:05:11.922
"I can't believe I've lost my poor little friend.

65
00:05:11.923 --> 00:05:18.124
I promised myself I'd take care of him until he was well."

66
00:05:18.125 --> 00:05:21.818
"Don't worry. I'm sure you'll find him.

67
00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:26.329
And one more thing," the servant said as he opened the door.

68
00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:28.829
"That fellow with the eye patch?

69
00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:33.153
He limped slightly and walked with a cane."

70
00:05:33.154 --> 00:05:38.028
"Oh no!" Miles groaned.

71
00:05:38.029 --> 00:05:43.501
"That man is probably the same brute who claimed that Edward was his son!"

72
00:05:43.502 --> 00:05:45.915
Miles stood up.

73
00:05:45.916 --> 00:05:51.124
He hated to leave his food, but he had to find Edward at once.

74
00:05:51.125 --> 00:05:57.070
The boy could be in trouble!

